			<string>SwiftPeek went Music-only at 0.2.1 after putting SpringBoard into Safe Mode. 0.4.0 allows SpringBoard again for recon only: ObjC-only, no hooks, no swizzles, no Swift metadata walks. Icon Inventory reads each app's artwork through UIKit (never SBIconModel) and records pixel statistics. Scan Windows walks the already-loaded view tree to tell UIKit surfaces from SwiftUI-hosted ones — that is what fills in Glyph's PENDING DUMP rows. Both need Target SpringBoard on, and all three default off. Respring after changing.</string>
